<title>MEXICO: Mexico's steel output hits record in March.</title>
<headline>Mexico's steel output hits record in March.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's steel output was a record 1.202 million tonnes in March, up 12 percent from the same month the year before, the National Iron and Steel Industry Chamber (Canacero) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Liquid steel production in the first quarter rose 7.6 percent to 3.470 million tonnes. </p>
<p>It gave the following breakdown of steel output:</p>
<p>				(Millions of tonnes)</p>
<p>				March 1997    March 1996   Change</p>
<p>Liquid Steel		 1.202	   1.073	  12.0 pct</p>
<p>Semi-finished		0.232	   0.170	  36.5 pct</p>
<p>Total Laminated	    0.875	   0.806	   8.6 pct</p>
<p>    -- Flat		  0.434	   0.395	   9.9 pct</p>
<p>    -- Non-Flat	    0.390	   0.356	   9.6 pct</p>
<p>    -- Other Laminated   0.051	   0.054	  -5.6 pct</p>
<p>((-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560))</p>
</text>
